{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"reasonable-kingsize-polliwog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe integration census attributes about 32.69 worker-phase seconds to partial-clone fixtures. The current fixture creates a real >100MiB object contrast and is duplicated per xdist worker. Closed cinderlike-weariful-angora deliberately requires proof that filter:blob:none is negotiated and omits a blob that materially distinguishes filtered from full history; that guard cannot be weakened or replaced by config inspection.\n\nA possible split is to retain one exact large-object guard and use a small real Git server/repository for protocol-only cases. Shared mutable servers may create races and cross-worker contamination, and no maintained-OSS consensus has yet been established.\n\n## Plan\n- Map each partial-clone test to protocol negotiation, missing-object, full-clone contrast, named/direct remote, standalone guard, reconvergence, and push behavior.\n- Freeze the one or more tests that require the >100MiB contrast.\n- Prototype isolated small fixtures only for cases whose failure oracle is independent of repository size; do not share mutable state across workers.\n- Seed negotiation, promisor, missing-object, and full-clone defects to prove equivalent detection.\n- Compare fixture setup, call time, macOS wall, and aggregate runner cost; survey maintained Git-heavy OSS suites.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The exact >100MiB filter contrast from cinderlike-weariful-angora remains covered by a real Git fixture.\n- [ ] Every smaller-fixture candidate is proven size-independent by an exact-defect mutation.\n- [ ] No mutable Git server or object database is shared across concurrent workers.\n- [ ] Before/after macOS wall and runner savings are measured.\n- [ ] Prior ticket constraints and at least three maintained OSS projects are recorded.\n- [ ] No production behavior or external Git protocol coverage is replaced by mocks.","id":"af11-aad5-bbe7-465a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","test-runtime","research","git"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Experiment with a small protocol fixture beside the required large partial-clone guard"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786827621345356001,"uuid":"cd4b778d-0b52-4514-9622-ecfed8dedb5c"}